<title>FINLAND: FINNISH FOREST INDUSTRY DENIES U.S. ACCUSATIONS.</title>
<headline>FINNISH FOREST INDUSTRY DENIES U.S. ACCUSATIONS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finnish Forest Industries Federation on Wednesday rejected claims by its U.S. counterpart, the American Forest and Paper Association, that it was trying to deny American producers access to European markets.</p>
<p>&quot;The Board of the Finnish Forest Industry Federation denies the Americans' claims. Finland is not opposing American market access in the EU. As a small country Finland has always favoured free and fair trade. Finland is not the leading force in the EU tariff policy and the tariff matter at large is an issue for the EU and US authorities,&quot; the Finnish federation said in a statement. --Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
